  "notes": [
    "Regular -AR verb — follows standard -AR endings with no exceptions",
    "Past participle: *agotado* (regular; also a very common adjective meaning \"exhausted/tired\" or \"sold out,\" depending on context)",
    "Means \"to exhaust/use up\" (resources, patience) or \"to run out of\" — *agotar las existencias* (to use up the stock), *agotar la paciencia* (to exhaust someone's patience)",
    "Reflexive *agotarse* is extremely common for \"to get tired out\" or \"to sell out\" — *me agoté después del entrenamiento* (I wore myself out after training), *las entradas se agotaron en minutos* (the tickets sold out in minutes)",
    "Related: *agotado/a* (exhausted; sold out), *agotamiento* (exhaustion), *agotador/a* (exhausting, tiring)"
  ],
